---
layout: app-layout.njk
title: Grade Pyramid – Climbing Logbook
discipline: true
bundle: performance-pyramid
staticShellNote: |-
  Genuinely static shell (#348), same pattern as public/map/index.html
         -- see that file's own comment for why every path below is absolute
         and client/performance-pyramid-main.js reads the username from
         location.pathname itself rather than this file being templated.
---
<div class="max-w-[960px] mx-auto">
  <!-- Picker/menu row before the brand row, and align-left on
       <climbing-header> -- matches /logbook's own layout (left-aligned
       brand row below the header row, not centered above it). Found via
       Raven's production report, 2026-08-10 -- see climbing-header.js's
       own comment on the align-left attribute. -->
  {% include "page-header.njk" %}

  <div class="flex items-end gap-3 mb-5" id="picker-tabs-row">
    <climbing-discipline-picker></climbing-discipline-picker>
    <climbing-tab-bar active-page="performance"></climbing-tab-bar>
  </div>

  <!-- #913 -- back-link utility (styles/tailwind.css), same pattern
       across every report page and My Account's own back links; href set
       client-side in client/performance-pyramid-main.js once USERNAME is known. -->
  <a class="back-link mt-4 mb-5" id="back-to-performance-link" href="#">
    <svg class="w-[.9rem] h-[.9rem] stroke-current fill-none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m15 18-6-6 6-6"></path></svg>
    Performance Insights
  </a>

  <h1 class="page-title">Grade Pyramid</h1>

  <!-- #601 -- shorter than the other 5 views' explainer block on
       purpose: <climbing-grade-pyramid> already renders its own rich
       "what this shows"/"how to read it" copy internally (#window-note,
       #health-card) -- this just adds the one thing that's missing,
       which field it's built from, without duplicating what the
       component already explains. -->
  <p class="text-[.78rem] text-muted mb-3" id="view-explainer">Built from every send's grade.</p>

  <!-- #737 -- which of this discipline's scales the pyramid below
       renders row grades in; client/report-grade-scale-picker.js, same
       shared per-discipline preference the trends/gap/rpe reports
       already use. No time-window control on this page (the pyramid's
       own "last 12 months" window is fixed, not a report control), so
       this sits alone rather than paired with one -- justify-end (not
       trends/gap/rpe's own justify-between) is this page's own correct
       call for that single-child case, not a copy-paste miss. #754 --
       dropped the one-off id (report-grade-scale-row): it was never
       queried by anything, and trends/gap/rpe's own equivalent wrapper
       has no id either -- keeping this div's own shape as close to
       theirs as its real, different content allows, rather than an easy
       trap for a future dev to copy from this page instead of them. -->
  <div class="flex justify-end mb-4">
    <div id="report-grade-scale-root"></div>
  </div>

  <!-- #111 -- Performance insights are online-only, deliberately, not a
       client-side fallback computed from possibly-stale cached entries
       (Raven's own call: at the crag with poor/no connection, the
       priority is reading/updating the logbook, not reviewing aggregate
       stats -- a "review later" activity). Shown instead of the pyramid
       when the initial fetch fails; starts hidden, toggled in
       performance-pyramid-main.js's own boot(). -->
  <div class="row-card text-center max-w-[420px] mx-auto" id="performance-offline" hidden>
    <p class="text-[.9rem] text-foreground">Performance insights need a connection.</p>
    <p class="text-[.82rem] text-muted mt-2">Reconnect and reload this page to see your Grade Pyramid.</p>
  </div>

  <!-- No visible heading here -- same "Grade Pyramid" tab-label-suffices
       reasoning as /logbook's own #panel-pyramid (see that file's
       comment); <climbing-grade-pyramid> renders its own window-note/
       pyramid-card/health-card into itself. -->
  <climbing-grade-pyramid></climbing-grade-pyramid>

  <div class="text-center text-muted text-[.78rem] mt-8" id="footer"></div>
</div>
